<title>JAPAN: Japan Ex-Im Bank guarantees Telecom Argentina loan.</title>
<headline>Japan Ex-Im Bank guarantees Telecom Argentina loan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Export-Import Bank of Japan said on Monday it had agreed to guarantee a private loan to Telecom Argentina STET for the upgrade and expansion of its telephone network.</p>
<p>The Ex-Im Bank said in a statement that the loan, worth $50 million from commercial banks led by Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi Ltd, would allow the firm to convert its telephone network into a digital network and install 38,000 new lines.</p>
<p>Telecom Argentina provides services to the northern part of the country.</p>
</text>
